(These tests measure the database's storage-layer throughput and latency through SQL-level operations. Each test uses a) Tj
T* (dedicated table populated with rows containing a random binary payload of the configured block size. The thread scaling sweep) Tj
T* (runs each workload at multiple concurrency levels to build a throughput-vs-concurrency curve, identifying the optimal thread) Tj
T* (count, saturation point, and Amdahl's serial fraction. All latency measurements are captured at the application layer \(including) Tj
T* (network round-trip time\) and reported as a full percentile distribution.) Tj
