(Executes UPDATE test_table SET payload = :random_data WHERE id = :random_pk under increasing thread concurrency. Each) Tj
T* (write operation involves: index seek to locate the target row, row-level lock acquisition, in-place page modification in the buffer) Tj
T* (pool, synchronous write-ahead log \(WAL/redo log\) flush to durable storage, and lock release. Writes are typically 2-5x slower) Tj
T* (than reads because every write must survive a crash -- the WAL flush is the serialization bottleneck all concurrent writers share.) Tj
T* (The scaling curve for writes directly reveals WAL throughput limits and lock contention behavior.) Tj
