(Writes random binary pages of configurable size \(matching the I/O block size\) along with their SHA-256 cryptographic hashes) Tj
T* (into the database under concurrent thread load. After all writes complete, a statistical sample of pages is read back, and the) Tj
T* (SHA-256 hash is recomputed and compared against the stored hash. This detects: silent storage-layer corruption \(bit rot\),) Tj
T* (network transport errors beyond what TCP/TLS checksums catch, database engine bugs in page management, and driver-level) Tj
T* (serialization issues. Any hash mismatch is a FAIL -- a critical finding indicating data corruption that should be investigated) Tj
T* (immediately.) Tj
