(Creates a set of bank accounts with known initial balances, then executes thousands of concurrent balance-transfer transactions) Tj
T* (\(debit account A, credit account B within a single BEGIN/COMMIT block\). After all transactions complete, the test verifies that) Tj
T* (SUM\(all_balances\) equals the original total -- the monetary conservation invariant. This tests the database's core ACID) Tj
T* (guarantees under realistic contention: atomicity \(partial transfers must not persist\), consistency \(balances must remain valid\),) Tj
T* (isolation \(concurrent transfers must not corrupt each other\), and durability \(committed transfers must survive\). The test also) Tj
T* (measures: transactions per second \(TPS\), deadlock frequency, commit latency distribution, and the ratio of successfully) Tj
T* (committed to total attempted transactions.) Tj
