(Executes SELECT payload FROM test_table WHERE id = :random_pk using randomly chosen primary keys across a scaling) Tj
T* (thread sweep \(e.g., 1, 2, 4, 8, 16, 32 threads\). Each operation exercises the full cloud database I/O path: B-tree clustered index) Tj
T* (seek \(O\(log n\) complexity\), single-page buffer pool fetch \(or storage-layer read on cache miss\), result serialization into the wire) Tj
T* (protocol \(TDS, PostgreSQL protocol, or MySQL protocol\), TLS record framing and encryption, and TCP network round-trip back) Tj
T* (to the client.) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (This is the fundamental performance primitive for cloud databases -- directly analogous to 4KB random read IOPS on block) Tj
T* (storage. The thread sweep builds a throughput-vs-concurrency curve that reveals the saturation point \(where adding connections) Tj
T* (stops improving IOPS\), the optimal thread count \(highest IOPS-per-connection\), and Amdahl's serial fraction \(the portion of the) Tj
T* (workload that cannot be parallelized\). Compare measured IOPS against your cloud tier's documented limits to determine) Tj
T* (headroom.) Tj
ET
BT
/F2 11 Tf
12.6499999999999986 TL
0.137 0.525 0.82 rg
51.0236220472441033 567.4962992125983874 Td
(Random Write \(I/O\)) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
9.7749999999999986 TL
0.314 0.333 0.373 rg
56.6929133858267775 550.4884251968503577 Td
(Executes UPDATE test_table SET payload = :random_data WHERE id = :random_pk under increasing thread concurrency. Each) Tj
T* (write involves: index seek to locate the target row, row-level lock acquisition \(or page lock on some engines\), in-place page) Tj
T* (modification in the buffer pool, synchronous write-ahead log \(WAL / redo log / transaction log\) flush to durable storage, and lock) Tj
T* (release.) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (Writes are typically 2-5× slower than reads because every write must survive a crash -- the synchronous WAL flush is the) Tj
T* (serialization bottleneck that all concurrent writers share. The thread scaling curve for writes directly reveals: WAL throughput) Tj
T* (limits, lock contention behavior under increasing concurrency, and the point at which adding connections increases latency) Tj
T* (without improving throughput. A high serial fraction \(> 0.15\) indicates the WAL is the binding constraint.) Tj
ET
BT
/F2 11 Tf
12.6499999999999986 TL
0.137 0.525 0.82 rg
51.0236220472441033 441.6380314960628652 Td
(Sequential Scan \(I/O\)) Tj
