/F1 8.5 Tf
9.7749999999999986 TL
0.314 0.333 0.373 rg
56.6929133858267775 424.6301574803148355 Td
(Executes SELECT * FROM test_table -- a full table scan reading every row in physical storage order. Unlike random I/O tests) Tj
T* (\(which are latency-bound by network RTT and index seeks\), sequential scan is bandwidth-bound -- it measures how fast the) Tj
T* (database can stream large result sets from storage through the buffer pool, across the network, and into the client.) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (Performance is determined by: storage sequential read throughput, buffer pool read-ahead efficiency \(how well the engine) Tj
T* (pre-fetches pages it knows it will need\), result set serialization speed, TCP window scaling behavior, and TLS encryption) Tj
T* (overhead on large payloads. The throughput \(MB/s\) should approach your cloud tier's documented sequential I/O bandwidth) Tj
T* (minus protocol overhead.) Tj
ET
BT
/F2 11 Tf
12.6499999999999986 TL
0.137 0.525 0.82 rg
51.0236220472441033 325.9844881889762291 Td
(Mixed Read/Write \(I/O\)) Tj
