BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
9.7749999999999986 TL
0.314 0.333 0.373 rg
56.6929133858267775 308.9766141732281994 Td
(Runs a concurrent mix of 70% point reads \(SELECT by PK\) and 30% single-row UPDATEs across multiple threads, simulating a) Tj
T* (realistic OLTP workload. This test reveals the read/write interference factor -- how much concurrent writes degrade read) Tj
T* (performance through buffer pool page invalidation, row-level lock contention, and WAL flush serialization.) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (The ratio of mixed IOPS to pure read IOPS quantifies this interference: a ratio near 1.0 means writes cause minimal disruption; a) Tj
T* (ratio below 0.6 indicates significant write-path contention that may require schema optimization \(e.g., covering indexes to avoid) Tj
T* (lookups\), workload isolation \(read replicas\), or tier upgrade \(faster log subsystem\). This is the most representative test for typical) Tj
T* (OLTP application performance.) Tj
ET
BT
/F2 11 Tf
12.6499999999999986 TL
0.137 0.525 0.82 rg
51.0236220472441033 210.3309448818895362 Td
(Bulk Insert \(I/O\)) Tj
