/F1 8.5 Tf
9.7749999999999986 TL
0.314 0.333 0.373 rg
56.6929133858267775 762.5199212598424765 Td
(Fires bursts of SELECT 1 queries at escalating concurrency levels \(1 → 5 → 10 → 20 → 40 → 60 → 80 → 100 → 150 →) Tj
T* (200 simultaneous connections\) to map the connection handling behavior under stress. At low concurrency, checkout latency) Tj
T* (should match the baseline ping. As concurrency increases, the test identifies: the saturation point \(where latency begins to spike) Tj
T* (due to connection pool exhaustion, database-side worker thread scheduling, or session memory pressure\), the failure threshold) Tj
T* (\(where new connections are refused with max_connections or login timeout errors\), and per-burst p50/p99 latency.) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (Use these results to size your application's max_pool_size parameter and to detect cloud-imposed connection limits that may not) Tj
T* (be documented. Many cloud database tiers silently throttle connections before reaching the advertised max_connections value.) Tj
ET
BT
/F2 11 Tf
12.6499999999999986 TL
0.137 0.525 0.82 rg
51.0236220472441033 663.8742519685039269 Td
(Data Integrity \(Stress\)) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
9.7749999999999986 TL
0.314 0.333 0.373 rg
56.6929133858267775 646.8663779527558972 Td
(Writes random binary pages of configurable size \(matching the I/O block size\) along with their SHA-256 cryptographic hashes) Tj
T* (into the database under concurrent thread load. After all writes complete, a statistical sample of pages is read back, the) Tj
T* (SHA-256 hash is recomputed from the retrieved binary data, and compared against the stored hash.) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (This detects: silent storage-layer corruption \(bit rot in the underlying cloud storage\), network transport errors beyond what) Tj
T* (TCP/TLS checksums catch \(such as memory corruption in network interface buffers\), database engine bugs in page) Tj
T* (management \(incorrect page splits, torn writes\), and driver-level serialization issues \(endianness problems, binary encoding) Tj
T* (errors\). SHA-256 has a collision probability of approximately 1 in 2^128, making false negatives effectively impossible.) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (Any hash mismatch is a FAIL -- a critical finding indicating data corruption somewhere in the end-to-end pipeline. This should be) Tj
T* (investigated immediately and escalated to the cloud provider if the storage layer is suspected.) Tj
ET
BT
/F2 11 Tf
12.6499999999999986 TL
0.137 0.525 0.82 rg
51.0236220472441033 517.6065354330708033 Td
(Concurrent Transactions \(Stress\)) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
9.7749999999999986 TL
0.314 0.333 0.373 rg
56.6929133858267775 500.5986614173227736 Td
(Creates a set of bank accounts with known initial balances, then executes thousands of concurrent balance-transfer transactions) Tj
T* (\(debit account A by $X, credit account B by $X within a single BEGIN/COMMIT block\). After all transactions complete, the test) Tj
T* (verifies that SUM\(all_balances\) equals the original total -- the monetary conservation invariant.) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (This tests the database's core ACID guarantees under realistic contention:) Tj
T* (• Atomicity -- partial transfers \(debit without credit\) must not persist after a crash or rollback) Tj
T* (• Consistency -- account balances must remain non-negative \(or at least the sum must be conserved\)) Tj
T* (• Isolation -- concurrent transfers must not see each other's intermediate states) Tj
T* (• Durability -- committed transfers must survive process termination) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (The test also measures: transactions per second \(TPS\), deadlock frequency and recovery, commit latency distribution \(p50/p99\),) Tj
T* (and the committed/total ratio. A balance drift > $0.01 is a FAIL indicating a serialization violation.) Tj
ET
BT
/F2 11 Tf
12.6499999999999986 TL
0.137 0.525 0.82 rg
51.0236220472441033 361.1340944881888504 Td
(Isolation Level Testing \(Stress\)) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
9.7749999999999986 TL
0.314 0.333 0.373 rg
56.6929133858267775 344.1262204724408207 Td
(Systematically tests each transaction isolation level supported by the database engine by executing known anomaly-producing) Tj
T* (patterns and checking whether the database correctly prevents them.) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (Isolation levels tested \(where supported\): READ UNCOMMITTED, READ COMMITTED, REPEATABLE READ, SERIALIZABLE,) Tj
T* (and SNAPSHOT.) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (Anomalies tested:) Tj
T* (• Dirty Read -- Transaction A reads uncommitted data written by Transaction B. Should be prevented at READ COMMITTED) Tj
T* (and above.) Tj
T* (• Non-Repeatable Read -- Transaction A reads a row, Transaction B modifies and commits it, Transaction A re-reads and gets) Tj
T* (different data. Should be prevented at REPEATABLE READ and above.) Tj
T* (• Phantom Read -- Transaction A executes a range query, Transaction B inserts a new row in that range and commits,) Tj
T* (Transaction A re-executes and sees the new row. Should be prevented at SERIALIZABLE.) Tj
T* (• Write Skew -- Two transactions read overlapping data, then make disjoint updates that together violate a constraint. Only) Tj
T* (prevented by SERIALIZABLE or explicit locking.) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (This validates that the database's actual behavior matches its documented isolation guarantees -- some cloud databases) Tj
T* (advertise SERIALIZABLE but implement it as snapshot isolation, which does not prevent write skew.) Tj
ET
BT
/F2 11 Tf
12.6499999999999986 TL
0.137 0.525 0.82 rg
51.0236220472441033 143.4333070866140361 Td
(Analytical Queries \(Decision Support\)) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
9.7749999999999986 TL
0.314 0.333 0.373 rg
56.6929133858267775 126.4254330708660063 Td
(Generates a normalized star-schema dataset \(zones, countries, vendors, buyers, products, inventory, sale orders, order details\)) Tj
T* (scaled by a configurable factor, then executes 16 original decision-support queries covering the full range of SQL optimizer code) Tj
T* (paths:) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (• Multi-way hash/merge/nested-loop joins across 4+ tables) Tj
T* (• Correlated subqueries with EXISTS and NOT EXISTS) Tj
T* (• Aggregation with GROUP BY, HAVING, CASE expressions) Tj
T* (• Common Table Expressions \(CTEs\) and derived tables) Tj
T* (• ORDER BY with LIMIT/TOP for ranking queries) Tj
T* (• LEFT JOIN distributions and NULL handling) Tj
T* (• Date range filtering and string pattern matching) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (Each query runs cold \(first execution -- no plan cache, cold buffer pool\) and warm \(immediate re-execution -- cached plan, warm) Tj
T* (buffer pool\) to measure plan compilation overhead and cache effectiveness. The cold/warm ratio reveals how much the) Tj
T* (optimizer's plan cache benefits your analytical workload.) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (Composite metrics: Geometric Mean \(exp\(Σ ln\(duration_i\) / N\)\) fairly weights all queries regardless of magnitude. Power Score) Tj
T* (\(\(3600 × Scale_Factor\) / Geometric_Mean\) normalizes throughput for cross-comparison across scale factors.) Tj
ET
